<title>KENYA: Kenyan coffee prices ease at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Kenyan coffee prices ease at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kenyan coffee prices were easier at the weekly coffee auction in Nairobi, auction officials said on Tuesday</p>
<p>&quot;Offerings were very mixed. A lot of it was end of season coffee,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Grade AAs $326 per 50-kg from $389 last week while grade ABs averaged $317 from $351. Grade PBs averaged $252 from $367.</p>
<p>The Coffee Board of Kenya sold 20,843 60-kg bags of coffee compared to 20,896 bags sold last week.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261</p>
